title: Evens only
golf: 45

Write `only_evens(nums)` that returns a new list with just the even numbers.
`only_evens([1, 2, 3, 4])` gives `[2, 4]`.
=== starter
def only_evens(nums):
    ...
=== broken
def only_evens(nums):
    result = []
    for n in nums:
        if n % 2:
            result.append(n)
    return result
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_only_evens(sol):
    eq(sol.only_evens([1, 2, 3, 4]), [2, 4], "only_evens([1, 2, 3, 4])")
    eq(sol.only_evens([7, 9]), [], "only_evens([7, 9])")
